-- title:
--   Derivative of the argument vector in time
-- statement:
--   For parameters $p\in\mathbb R^d$ and a position $x\in\mathbb R^3$, consider the argument vector $s\mapsto(s,x_0,x_1,x_2,p_0,\dots,p_{d-1})\in\mathbb R^{4+d}$. At every $t$,
--   $$
--   \frac{d}{ds}\Big|_{s=t}(s,x,p)=e_0,
--   $$
--   the unit vector of the time coordinate.
--
--   By the chain rule, the time derivative of a parametrized field is the coordinate derivative of its elementary representation in coordinate $0$.
